  "pli-tv-bu-vb-pj3:1.3.9": "I have here translated <i lang='pi' translate='no'>kāya</i> as breath in accordance with the usage in the Ānāpānasati Sutta (<a href='https://suttacentral.net/mn118/en/brahmali#24.6'>MN 118:24.6</a>) where the breath is specifically said to be a body among bodies. Sp 1.165: <i lang='pi' translate='no'>Sakalassa assāsakāyassa ādimajjhapariyosānaṁ viditaṁ karonto pākaṭaṁ karonto “assasissāmī”ti sikkhati</i>, “He trains, ‘I will breathe in’, producing knowledge of and familiarity with the beginning, the middle, and the end of the whole body of the breath.” ",
